WEBVTT

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.450
Yuya and Reiji Akaba's match ended suddenly.

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:11.490
When Reiji Akaba used Pendulum 
Summon, Yuya was shocked.

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:14.300
Well done, Yuya.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:18.800
I've told you everything 
I needed to tell you.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:23.350
Principal!

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:25.840
Hot-Blooded Shuzo Theater
The End

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:32.800
Due to my dad's hot-blooded 
training, Yuya got his smile back.

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:37.450
But I'm the one who has to train harder.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:42.820
If I was able to defeat Masumi 
Koutsu in the LDS battle...

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:46.570
I can't stay like this!

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:53.230
Implementing mass into Solid 
Vision has created Action Duels.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:01:01.410
In duels where the field, monsters and duelists 
become one, the people are caught in a frenzy of excitement!

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:05.410
Believe x Believe  Biri-Biri-Biri Buddies!

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:24.190
You!  The strongest card 
isn't about winning or losing

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:27.600
You!  At full speed  On the game

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.340
Swinging ma ma ma mind

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:40.910
The soul's pendulum  Ultimate confusion

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.110
Impulse  Got it got it

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:48.320
Tough battles  Real revolution

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:59.080
Everybody goin'  Break through the walls!

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:06.000
Infinite future  Get rid of indecision!

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:09.940
Make it Make it  Be courageous (Break it now)

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:13.340
Step ahead!  Take a step (Do it now)

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:23.620
The fun is only getting started!  
So everyone's a Believer!!

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:26.960
Believe x Believe  Biri-Biri-Biri Buddies!

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:37.000
Go for the Junior Youth Championship!!

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:45.240
Watch me, Dad.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:50.540
I'll polish my skills even more so 
that I can become a pro like you.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:54.320
A duelist whose awesome entertainment 
dueling brings smiles to everyone's faces!

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:57.210
Time to eat!

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.390
I'll do it!

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:01.530
I'll definitely become a pro!

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:05.520
Eat or talk, choose one!

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:09.700
Here.

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:11.430
Sawatari!

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:15.300
You're so disgusting in front of a lady.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:18.940
Your eating and dueling are both disgusting.

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:20.180
Disgusting?

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:23.790
You're right about my eating, but 
what's disgusting about my dueling?

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:27.590
You assaulted someone again.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:30.720
It wasn't Yuya!

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:32.560
What do you mean, "again?"

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:39.300
Someone using Xyz Summon 
attacked a LDS teacher.

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:42.400
Reiji!

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:45.030
Hey!

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.470
We'll finish this another time.

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:49.120
That's why he suddenly left.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:51.980
I was kidding when I said 
you assaulted someone.

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:55.430
The victim was a LDS teacher.

00:03:55.430 --> 00:04:00.230
Even with your unfair Pendulum Summon, 
you couldn't have defeated him.

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:01.560
Unfair?

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:03.920
What's unfair about Pendulum?

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:09.900
It's unfair that only 
you have Pendulum Cards.

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:14.180
But that's just for now.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:19.340
It's rumored that Leo Corporation 
is developing Pendulum Cards.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:25.920
I'll get those cards first 
and use them to defeat you.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:28.410
That's all I wanted to say.

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:31.350
See ya.  I'll wait for you in 
the Junior Youth Championship.

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:34.270
Junior Youth Championship?

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:37.120
Oh yeah!

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:39.300
That means I can't become a pro!

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:46.190
Yuya!  Yuzu!

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:47.830
You're done with classes!

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:49.560
Let's go to You Show School!

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:55.740
What's wrong, Yuya?

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:58.100
You can't enter...

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:00.050
...the Junior Youth Championship?

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:01.610
That's right.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:10.720
In order to enter the championship, I need at least 50 
official Junior Youth Class matches this year with a 60% win rate.

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:13.560
What's your record this year?

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:16.630
46 matches, 26 wins.

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:20.300
26 divided by 46 is...

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:22.720
56.5% win rate.

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:24.500
That isn't good enough.

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:26.590
Tatsuya, you're good at math.

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:31.160
But if you've only had 46 matches, 
you still have 4 left to get to 50.

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:36.420
If you win them all, you'll have 
30 wins, which is exactly 60%.

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:38.540
That's true.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:43.390
We searched the school for 
four opponents, but...

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:45.030
No way.

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:48.670
Why should I duel against 
someone who defeated a pro?

00:05:48.670 --> 00:05:52.900
You're entering the Junior Youth Championship 
when you're good enough to defeat Strong Ishijima?

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:54.100
You must be kidding.

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:58.050
Since you beat the champion, don't you get a 
free pass to enter the Junior Youth Championship?

00:05:58.050 --> 00:05:59.570
You're lucky.

00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:01.960
I don't get a free pass!

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:06.080
That wasn't an official 
match, and I'm not a pro.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:08.410
Everyone has the wrong idea.

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:12.500
In order to become a pro, you have to 
win in the Junior Youth Championship.

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:16.410
And then pass the Youth Qualification 
Test and win in the Youth Championship.

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:19.210
And then pass the Pro Test.

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:22.260
And I can't even take the 
important first step!

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:28.140
Dammit!  I'll do whatever it takes 
to find four people and duel them!

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:31.830
1, 2, 3, 4.

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:34.630
No way.

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:35.470
NG.

00:06:35.470 --> 00:06:36.500
Why not?

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:39.700
We're still in elementary school, 
so we're in Junior Class.

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:41.700
Junior Youth is for middle school students.

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:44.990
Then let me duel you, Yuzu!

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:46.360
I refuse.

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:47.790
Why?

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:51.210
Because I've already qualified.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:55.470
Besides, we've already had plenty 
of practice duels together.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:58.100
Then who's left?

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:00.400
Why don't you have Gongenzaka help you again?

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:08.780
You almost have 50 matches because he helped you 
by letting you battle Gongenzaka Dojo's students.

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:11.430
Yeah.  I'm thankful for that.

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:15.070
He helps me all the time.

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:20.250
It's thanks to Gongenzaka that 
I can even try to become a pro.

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:26.690
But that's why I don't want 
to rely on him anymore.

00:07:27.470 --> 00:07:32.660
I need to become stronger on my own so 
that Gongenzaka can rely on me instead.

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:35.870
Stronger on my own...

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:38.010
You're right.

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:41.340
Hey, what's up?

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:43.250
It's nothing!

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:46.320
I just want to become stronger!

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.300
Stronger?

00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:49.120
Yuzu?

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:50.270
What about the school?

00:07:50.450 --> 00:07:53.610
Tell my dad that I can't go today!

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:56.050
What's with Yuzu?

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:59.250
Maybe because you only praised Gongenzaka.

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:03.210
You didn't thank Yuzu.

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:05.870
That wasn't good, Yuya.

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:10.270
I'm thankful to both Yuzu and Gongenzaka!

00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:12.360
Actually, more for Yuzu!

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:13.810
Too late.

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:20.990
Yuya is trying to change, so 
I can't stay the same either.

00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:25.650
I have to become stronger so that 
I can protect You Show School.

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:34.430
I said that I wouldn't rely on Gongenzaka, 
but how will I find four more duelists?

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:38.760
Oh my boy!

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:41.340
It's been awhile, Yuya!

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:42.190
You're...

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:43.640
Nico Smiley!

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:45.390
Why are you here?

00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:47.740
He brought good news.

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:49.300
Be happy, Yuya!

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:53.610
You're free to enter the 
Junior Youth Championship!

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:55.580
Free to enter?

00:08:55.580 --> 00:08:57.700
That's right, Yuya!

00:08:57.700 --> 00:09:01.650
Even though it was only an exhibition 
match, you did defeat Strong Ishijima.

00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:08.560
The Maiami Duel Association recognized your skills, so you 
received special permission to enter the Junior Youth Championship!

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:10.010
Incredible!

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:11.960
Congratulations, Yuya!

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:13.890
The Duel Association approved you!

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:15.870
That gives me shivers!

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:18.200
What's wrong?

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:21.610
Well, I'm thankful, but...

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:26.320
Since you beat the champion, don't you get a 
free pass to enter the Junior Youth Championship?

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:28.810
I don't need a free pass.

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:32.320
Why?  Why?

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:34.940
Because it feels like cheating.

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:37.070
No, it's not cheating!

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:40.560
The Association approved 
it.  You should feel proud.

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:43.790
It also feels like I'm doing Ishijima wrong.

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:46.360
I haven't seen him recently.

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:48.320
How's the champion doing?

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:51.650
He's no longer champion.

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:56.680
He relinquished the title after that match.

00:09:56.680 --> 00:10:02.050
He said that he had to redo his training 
from scratch and went overseas to train.

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:06.140
Therefore, I'm a free agent.

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:10.590
I have no duelist to manage!

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:16.500
So Yuya, let's reach the top together!

00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:17.250
No thanks.

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:20.320
I see.

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:22.630
That's why you negotiated 
with the Association.

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:25.070
So that you can make money for yourself.

00:10:25.070 --> 00:10:26.500
You're the worst.

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:27.920
You're wrong!

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:32.140
It's because I adore Yuya's talent!

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:37.300
If you do, then I have a request.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:39.250
Request?

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:48.760
I didn't expect him to be 
Leo Corporation's president.

00:10:49.070 --> 00:10:52.320
Does that mean he's the chairman's son?

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:56.100
Security is very tight.

00:10:56.100 --> 00:11:01.160
If I ask to see the President, 
I don't think they'll let me.

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:08.760
Aww, I want to duel him!

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:10.650
I knew you'd be here!

00:11:11.340 --> 00:11:15.920
You haven't come to our school 
because you're after Reiji Akaba!

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:18.900
No, uhh...  "after him" 
isn't the right word...

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:21.300
It's the same when you went after Yuya.

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:24.540
When someone catches your eye, 
you stick to him immediately!

00:11:25.390 --> 00:11:27.340
Because he seems fun!

00:11:27.340 --> 00:11:32.840
He uses Fusion, Synchro and 
Xyz, and he now uses Pendulum!

00:11:33.070 --> 00:11:36.810
But you can't get near him easily.

00:11:36.810 --> 00:11:39.830
Because he's the president 
of Leo Corporation.

00:11:39.830 --> 00:11:41.610
So you do know.

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:43.650
Anyway, come with me.

00:11:43.650 --> 00:11:46.140
Hey, where are we going?

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:46.760
C'mon!

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:48.270
Tell me!

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:57.560
Rumors say that the attack 
occurred around here.

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:01.650
This is the only place that looks suspicious.

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:05.210
Is there something they 
don't want to show us?

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:11.960
Hey, Masumi...

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:14.410
What are you doing here?

00:12:14.720 --> 00:12:16.140
It's a uniformed official!

00:12:16.140 --> 00:12:18.230
We're not bad people!

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:24.720
I'm Masumi Koutsu, and I took Professor 
Marco's Fusion Course at Leo Duel School.

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:25.870
Marco?

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:26.460
And you?

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:30.730
I'm Synchro Course's Yaiba Toudou.

00:12:30.940 --> 00:12:33.610
I'm Xyz Course's Hokuto Shijima.

00:12:36.410 --> 00:12:38.640
You three are students of the school?

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:39.840
Yes!

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:43.540
I see.  You heard what happened here?

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:44.760
No.

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:47.790
We only heard that someone 
attacked Professor Marco.

00:12:47.790 --> 00:12:52.360
The LDS head office said that we 
couldn't see the Professor yet.

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:55.340
We want to know what happened!

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:59.300
Did someone attack him in a duel?

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:02.230
It's rumored that the culprit is an Xyz user.

00:13:02.230 --> 00:13:07.030
As a fellow Xyz user, when I hear 
that someone is using it for evil...

00:13:07.030 --> 00:13:12.720
Sorry, but I can't talk about specifics 
because we're still investigating.

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:16.050
Is Professor Marco okay?

00:13:16.050 --> 00:13:18.410
I can't answer that either.  Sorry.

00:13:19.870 --> 00:13:22.380
Don't worry.

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:27.870
The LDS higher-ups will uncover the truth.

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:32.410
You should work on polishing 
your dueling skills like usual.

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:36.630
I think that would make 
Professor Marco happy.

00:13:36.990 --> 00:13:38.010
Okay?

00:13:38.010 --> 00:13:42.590
Leave this place to us and go back to school.

00:13:43.030 --> 00:13:44.100
Okay!

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:45.790
Okay.

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:53.120
The uniformed officials are cool!

00:13:53.120 --> 00:13:58.850
They're a super elite squad that 
passed the pro test with top scores.

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:01.870
I want to wear that uniform soon too!

00:14:01.870 --> 00:14:04.490
I want to be in LDS's Top Team!

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:09.470
Where are you going on your own again?

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:11.210
You guys can go back!

00:14:11.210 --> 00:14:12.800
I'll search somewhere else!

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:14.940
Search?

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:16.670
Sheesh...

00:14:19.430 --> 00:14:23.070
Why did you bring me here?

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:34.940
Please teach me how to Fusion Summon!

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:36.320
Here?

00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:37.030
Yes.

00:14:37.030 --> 00:14:38.450
Why?

00:14:38.450 --> 00:14:39.920
I want to become stronger!

00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:42.010
I'm not good enough right now!

00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:46.670
Umm...  Are you upset 
about losing to that girl?

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:49.610
I got it!

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:56.540
You were fooled by a fake 
image in the crystal.

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:59.950
Your eyes must be very cloudy.

00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:07.790
Reiji Akaba said we would finish 
our battle another time.

00:15:07.790 --> 00:15:11.610
I want the strength to 
protect You Show School!

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:13.610
I want to defeat Masumi Koutsu!

00:15:13.610 --> 00:15:14.540
That's why...

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:18.850
You want to learn Fusion Summoning 
from a fellow Fusion user.

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:20.010
Correct?

00:15:20.010 --> 00:15:22.850
Yes!  So please teach me!

00:15:23.430 --> 00:15:25.160
What should I do?

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:27.250
You can't?

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:29.520
It's not that I can't...

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:30.910
Am I allowed?

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:33.960
Because if I teach you, you'll 
definitely become stronger.

00:15:33.960 --> 00:15:35.390
Then that's good!

00:15:35.390 --> 00:15:38.810
Make me so strong that I 
won't lose against anyone!

00:15:38.810 --> 00:15:42.050
But...  Am I allowed?

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:48.940
Here.  This card is Polymerization.

00:15:48.940 --> 00:15:53.470
You use this spell card to fuse 
specific monsters together.

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:56.900
That's the most basic fact about 
Fusion Summoning.  Understand?

00:15:56.900 --> 00:15:58.500
Yeah.  I understand.

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:00.940
I can't believe I'm actually teaching her.

00:16:00.940 --> 00:16:04.760
My kindness is my greatest flaw.

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:09.700
The Fusion Material Monsters can 
be on the field or in my hand?

00:16:09.700 --> 00:16:11.960
Huh?  Oh, yeah they can.

00:16:11.960 --> 00:16:17.560
What's important is that the Fusion Material 
Monsters are all in one or the other.

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:19.560
But there are exceptions.

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:27.340
When I activate Polymerization, I send my Fusion Material Monsters 
to my graveyard and bring out my Fusion Monster from my Extra Deck.

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:28.360
That's right.

00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:33.030
What is it?

00:16:38.190 --> 00:16:39.380
What?

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:02.470
Who are you?

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:06.940
You're not from here, are you?

00:17:06.940 --> 00:17:08.230
Neither are you.

00:17:09.390 --> 00:17:12.010
You're the guy from before!

00:17:12.360 --> 00:17:13.880
Yuzu, you know him?

00:17:14.410 --> 00:17:17.390
When I was here with Sawatari...

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:19.920
Xyz Summon!

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:25.320
Rank 4 Dark Rebellion Xyz Dragon!

00:17:28.850 --> 00:17:31.790
Are you behind this incident too?

00:17:33.470 --> 00:17:34.940
Incident?

00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:37.940
Someone attacked an LDS teacher.

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:39.740
LDS...

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:44.450
So that's why security was tight.

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:47.910
You're the culprit?

00:17:51.390 --> 00:17:53.740
Who are you?

00:17:54.320 --> 00:17:57.960
Did you duel Sawatari to save me?

00:17:57.960 --> 00:18:00.500
Or because you hate LDS?

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:01.520
That's...

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:03.700
You're the culprit?

00:18:04.940 --> 00:18:06.540
Masumi Koutsu!

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:08.270
What did you do to Professor Marco?

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:09.340
Answer me!

00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:11.700
Why are you also here?

00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:15.470
I thought I'd find something by 
going to the first crime scene.

00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:19.180
If you're here, you saved me 
the trouble of finding you!

00:18:19.650 --> 00:18:21.080
Wait a second!

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:23.390
I'm still talking with him!

00:18:23.390 --> 00:18:25.210
Mine is more important!

00:18:25.210 --> 00:18:26.590
What are you talking about?

00:18:26.590 --> 00:18:29.960
Besides, we don't know if he's the culprit!

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:33.830
We'll know by finding out 
whether he's a Xyz user!

00:18:33.830 --> 00:18:37.060
Xyz?  Oh really.

00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:42.320
I'll check!  Battle me!

00:18:42.320 --> 00:18:43.790
Let's duel!

00:18:43.790 --> 00:18:46.760
Stop it!  That's enough!

00:18:57.180 --> 00:18:59.650
He's gone.

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:04.540
It's the same as last time.

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:06.010
Hey, Yuzu!

00:19:06.010 --> 00:19:07.390
Answer me if you're here!

00:19:07.390 --> 00:19:08.410
Yuya!

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:10.140
Yuzu!

00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:14.010
The principal was worried, 
so he told me to find you.

00:19:14.010 --> 00:19:17.870
Why didn't you answer your phone?  
Why did you come here again?

00:19:17.870 --> 00:19:19.390
Yuya Sakaki!

00:19:19.390 --> 00:19:21.140
I knew you were part of his team!

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:22.800
You're...

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:24.450
Sora is here too?

00:19:24.940 --> 00:19:26.990
Where did he go?

00:19:26.990 --> 00:19:27.910
Who?

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:29.340
Stop playing dumb!

00:19:29.340 --> 00:19:30.810
Bring him out!

00:19:30.810 --> 00:19:33.070
Who are you talking about?

00:19:33.070 --> 00:19:34.480
Stop it!

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:36.230
You really don't know?

00:19:36.230 --> 00:19:37.520
You too?

00:19:37.520 --> 00:19:38.990
What are you talking about?

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:42.590
He also vanished last time when Yuya arrived.

00:19:43.250 --> 00:19:44.500
He?

00:19:44.760 --> 00:19:46.720
Bring him out already!

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:48.010
Over there!

00:19:48.520 --> 00:19:49.590
I just saw him!

00:19:49.590 --> 00:19:51.170
He fled that way!

00:19:51.170 --> 00:19:54.100
If you don't hurry up and chase 
him, he's going to escape again!

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:55.900
Damn!  I won't let him escape!

00:19:57.070 --> 00:19:58.610
Was someone there?

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:00.210
I was lying.

00:20:00.210 --> 00:20:03.360
She was interfering with our training.

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:06.050
Training?  Here with Yuzu?

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:09.070
Yeah.  Yuzu said that next time-

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:15.230
Is it a secret to Yuya that you're 
learning Fusion Summoning from me?

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:17.340
Yuzu is learning Fusion?

00:20:18.520 --> 00:20:21.210
For the Junior Youth Championship?

00:20:22.050 --> 00:20:23.190
By the way, Yuzu...

00:20:23.190 --> 00:20:25.650
I found four opponents!

00:20:25.650 --> 00:20:31.210
Actually, Nico Smiley is 
going to find them for me.

00:20:31.650 --> 00:20:33.810
I see.  That's good.

00:20:33.810 --> 00:20:36.670
Yeah.  All I have to do is win!

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:40.050
I swear I'll enter the 
Junior Youth Championship!

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:43.340
Hey, what's this championship 
you're talking about?

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:44.810
Can I enter too?

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:47.470
I don't know...

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:50.650
Since arriving at Maiami City, 
you haven't had 50 matches yet.

00:20:50.650 --> 00:20:53.730
You need at least that many 
matches and 30 victories.

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:55.270
So I can't enter?

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:59.360
But I want to enter with you, Yuya!

00:20:59.830 --> 00:21:07.550
Even if you don't have enough matches, there's a stipulation 
where you're allowed to enter if you have no losses and 6 wins in a row.

00:21:07.790 --> 00:21:09.830
Really?  Hooray!

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:12.810
I can defeat six opponents easily!

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:18.060
Ask that Nico guy to find 
six opponents for me!

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:19.790
Sure.

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:22.830
I see.

00:21:22.830 --> 00:21:26.560
Yuzu learned from that match that 
she wants to become stronger.

00:21:27.030 --> 00:21:28.760
I see it.

00:21:28.760 --> 00:21:32.200
I see that Pendulum Summon 
can evolve even further.

00:21:33.340 --> 00:21:35.610
I don't want to lose to him either.

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:41.230
I don't know what Reiji Akaba saw beyond 
Pendulum, but I'll find out too!

00:21:43.300 --> 00:21:45.030
This is the second time.

00:21:46.390 --> 00:21:50.920
What's happening around me?

00:22:12.460 --> 00:22:17.940
Catch the dream dancing in my heart
Release my falling tears

00:22:18.160 --> 00:22:27.420
I'll step out on to my first field
To meet my miracle  Fabulous One Step

00:22:34.310 --> 00:22:39.430
I realized that strength can't be given

00:22:39.690 --> 00:22:44.670
It's something I have to grab myself

00:22:44.960 --> 00:22:50.110
In that case, I have to keep moving
I can't stay still

00:22:50.360 --> 00:22:55.370
Even if walls and headwinds block my way

00:22:55.570 --> 00:23:00.970
I'll draw my trump card called 
"courage" to take a step forward

00:23:00.970 --> 00:23:05.390
I believe in my story of victory

00:23:05.680 --> 00:23:11.360
Everyone during battle is My Way
Duelists are being tested

00:23:11.360 --> 00:23:16.770
When times are tough, that's when you 
Smile, Jump, Fight & Step Up!

00:23:16.770 --> 00:23:22.070
Your smile is your Energy
Kick away your feelings of running away

00:23:22.070 --> 00:23:31.440
Jump into the new field
Shiny One Step that leads to the future

00:23:32.440 --> 00:23:39.660
One step... Just one step is fine
That's your Big Chance!!

00:23:44.630 --> 00:23:47.540
Starting today, I promise 
to win my four matches!

00:23:47.540 --> 00:23:49.580
Mom, is breakfast ready?

00:23:49.580 --> 00:23:56.100
She's excited about using Michy's recipe to 
make mille-feuille pork cutlets, so it's taking time.

00:23:56.100 --> 00:23:58.920
What?  But I'm hungry!

00:23:59.300 --> 00:24:05.300
I'll serve you up with a Cooking 
Duel based on my perfect recipes.

00:24:05.300 --> 00:24:06.490
Cooking Duel?

00:24:06.720 --> 00:24:11.430
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V:
Genius Cook Michio Mokota

00:24:11.430 --> 00:24:13.410
The fun is only getting started!
